uage agents. Presented as a spotlight paper at ICLR 2024, Sotopia provides a platform where agents can interact with each other and the environment in complex social scenarios.\\n\\n## Key Features\\n\\n- **Open-ended Environment**: Easily extensible to include new environments and agents\\n- **Social Intelligence Evaluation**: Designed specifically for assessing social capabilities in language agents\\n- **Scalable Architecture**: Supports large numbers of agents and environments\\n- **Interactive Learning**: Agents learn through social interactions and environmental feedback\\n\\n## Installation\\n\\n### Prerequisites\\n- Python 3.11+\\n- Conda environment (recommended)\\n- OpenAI API key\\n\\n### Quick Installation\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash\\nconda create -n sotopia python=3.11\\nconda activate sotopia\\ncurl -sSL https://install.python-poetry.org | python3\\npython -m pip install sotopia\\nsotopia install\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n### Environment Setup\\nSet your OpenAI API key:\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash\\nconda env config vars set OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### Easy Sample Server\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`python\\nimport asyncio\\nfrom sotopia.samplers import UniformSampler\\nfrom sotopia.server import run_async_server\\n\\nasyncio.run(\\n    run_async_server(\\n        model_dict={\\n            \"env\": \"gpt-4\",\\n            \"agent1\": \"gpt-4o-mini\", \\n            \"agent2\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\\n        },\\n        sampler=UniformSampler(),\\n    )\\n)\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\nOr run the minimalist demo:\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash\\npython examples/minimalist_demo.py\\n\\\\`\\\\`\\\\`\\n\\n## Code Structure\\n\\nThe Sotopia repository contains several key directories:\\n\\n- \\\\`sotopia/\\\\` - Core library code\\n- \\\\`sotopia-chat/\\\\` - Chat interface components\\n- \\\\`examples/\\\\` - Usage examples and demos\\n- \\\\`notebooks/\\\\` - Jupyter notebook tutorials\\n- \\\\`tests/\\\\` - Test suite\\n- \\\\`docs/\\\\` - Documentation